WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.109
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:10.817
This lesson covers objective 2 point 3.

00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:15.884
Given a scenario, select and configure wireless devices and technologies.

00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:21.230
Today's concept: matching Wi-Fi generations to standards, bands and features.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.370
Here are the recent generations, from Wi-Fi four to Wi-Fi seven.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.487
Each has an IEEE standard behind it.

00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:33.970
Eight oh two dot eleven N, A C, A X, and B E.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.471
Wi-Fi six uses the two point four and five gigahertz bands.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:43.491
Wi-Fi six E is the same standard, extended into the six gigahertz band.

00:00:43.491 --> 00:00:45.400
Wi-Fi seven uses all three.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.284
Two features separate them.

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:53.621
BSS coloring is a Wi-Fi six feature, it tags frames so an access point can ignore a neighbor on the same channel.

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:56.200
Multi-link operation arrives with Wi-Fi seven.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.645
So ax is Wi-Fi six, not seven.

00:00:59.645 --> 00:01:02.395
And five gigahertz is not the new band.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.510
The new band is six gigahertz.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.331
For the exam, eight oh two dot eleven A X is Wi-Fi six.

00:01:10.331 --> 00:01:12.471
Six E adds the six gigahertz band.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:17.443
Eight oh two dot eleven B E is Wi-Fi seven, and it brings multi-link operation.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.520
That's objective two point three.
